From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:51:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] L2 cache for code only: DMA buffers maintained in the L2
 too (test version)

Review of the code-only version: RAM is executable, so a speculative instruction fetch can bring
a line of a DMA buffer into the L2, and data hits that line even though data can't allocate. So
every DMA transfer now also cleans and invalidates its buffer in the L2, as the data version does
(upstream a2f8bc51, 260ac76c): SD read before and after, SD write, OLED. The FatFS window and file
buffers sit on their own cache lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/RZA1/cache/cache.c                 | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/RZA1/cache/cache.h                 |  3 ++
 src/RZA1/oled/oled_low_level.c         |  3 +-
 src/RZA1/sdhi/src/sd/access/sd_read.c  |  7 +++--
 src/RZA1/sdhi/src/sd/access/sd_write.c |  3 +-
 src/deluge/hid/display/oled.cpp        |  3 +-
 src/fatfs/ff.h                         |  4 +--
 7 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/RZA1/cache/cache.c b/src/RZA1/cache/cache.c
index bc9235b8..ec698fbd 100644
--- a/src/RZA1/cache/cache.c
+++ b/src/RZA1/cache/cache.c
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 Includes   <System Includes> , "Project Includes"
 ******************************************************************************/
 #include "RZA1/cache/cache.h"
+
+#include "RZA1/compiler/asm/inc/asm.h"
 #include "RZA1/system/iodefine.h"
 #include "RZA1/system/r_typedefs.h"
 
@@ -240,8 +242,8 @@ void L2CacheFlushAll(void)
 void L2CacheEnable(void)
 {
     L2C.REG2_INT_CLEAR   = 0x000001FFuL; /* Clear the reg2_int_raw_status register */
-    /* Data never allocates in the L2 (all ways locked for data): DMA buffers stay coherent with the L1 maintenance
-       alone. Only instruction fetches fill it. */
+    /* Data never allocates in the L2 (all ways locked for data). Only instruction fetches fill it. A speculative one
+       can still bring in a line of a DMA buffer, so DMA transfers maintain the L2 too (invalidate_range_all_caches()). */
     L2C.REG9_D_LOCKDOWN0 = 0xFFFFFFFFuL;
     L2C.REG9_I_LOCKDOWN0 = 0x00000000uL;
 
@@ -290,4 +292,41 @@ void L2CacheCleanFlushAllAndDisable(void)
     L2CacheDisable();
 }
 
+/******************************************************************************
+ * Function Name: L2CacheCleanInvalidateRange
+ * Description  : Clean and invalidate the L2 cache lines of a range (by physical address, which is the
+ *                virtual one here).
+ * Arguments    : start - start address
+ *                end   - end address (exclusive)
+ * Return Value : none
+ ******************************************************************************/
+void L2CacheCleanInvalidateRange(uintptr_t start, uintptr_t end)
+{
+    uint32_t addr = start & ~31uL;
+    while (addr < end)
+    {
+        L2C.REG7_CLEAN_INV_PA = addr;
+        while (L2C.REG7_CLEAN_INV_PA & 1uL)
+        {
+        }
+        addr += 32;
+    }
+    L2C.REG7_CACHE_SYNC = 0;
+}
+
+/******************************************************************************
+ * Function Name: invalidate_range_all_caches
+ * Description  : A DMA buffer, before and after the transfer: dirty lines written back through L1 and L2, then
+ *                both emptied for the range.
+ * Arguments    : start - start address
+ *                end   - end address (exclusive)
+ * Return Value : none
+ ******************************************************************************/
+void invalidate_range_all_caches(uintptr_t start, uintptr_t end)
+{
+    v7_dma_flush_range(start, end);
+    L2CacheCleanInvalidateRange(start, end);
+    v7_dma_inv_range(start, end);
+}
+
 /* End of File */
